{"position":"12:36/q07/p1","rows":["DAMGHANI:v1p20/r1"],"prefer":[],"against":[],"reasons_add":"Al-Dāmaghānī explicitly identifies the wine dreamer as the king's cupbearer."}
{"question":"12:36/q05","position":"They are literally young men accompanying Joseph into prison.","reasons":"Al-Dāmaghānī glosses the two fityān as the young men who entered alongside Joseph.","rows":["DAMGHANI:v1p347/r15","DAMGHANI:v1p350/r2"],"prefer":[],"against":[]}
{"position":"12:36/q23/p2","rows":["DAMGHANI:v1p146/r3"],"prefer":[],"against":[],"reasons_add":"Al-Dāmaghānī cites the bread above the head as an instance of literal carrying."}
{"position":"12:36/q24/p1","rows":["DAMGHANI:v1p362/r14"],"prefer":[],"against":[],"reasons_add":"Al-Dāmaghānī explicitly gives physical elevation above the head as a sense of fawq."}
{"position":"12:36/q31/p1","rows":["DAMGHANI:v1p59/r1","IBNJAWZI-NUZHA:v1p218/r1","IBNJAWZI-NUZHA:v1p218/r2"],"prefer":[],"against":[],"reasons_add":"Al-Dāmaghānī and Ibn al-Jawzī give dream interpretation as a sense of taʾwīl; Ibn al-Jawzī also cites the dream's later fulfillment in 12:100."}
{"position":"12:36/q22/p1","rows":["IBNJINNI-MUHTASAB:v1p19/r2"],"prefer":[],"against":[],"reasons_add":"The Muḥtasab preface specifically notes Ibn Jinnī's defense of Ibn ʿAbbās's ʿinaban wording."}
{"position":"12:36/q21/p2","rows":["IBNJINNI-MUHTASAB:v1p19/r2","BURHAN:v2p277/r11","BURHAN:v2p277/r9","ITQAN:v3p101/r3"],"prefer":[],"against":[],"reasons_add":"Ibn Jinnī treats wine as the grapes' effect, named in place of its cause; al-Zarkashī describes the grapes by their future wine, and al-Suyūṭī compares other things named by their future state."}
{"position":"12:36/q21/p1","rows":["BURHAN:v2p277/r10","ITQAN:v2p378/r11"],"prefer":[],"against":[],"reasons_add":"Al-Zarkashī relays Ibn Durayd through al-Fārisī on the Azd Oman lexical usage and a view denying metaphor on that basis; al-Suyūṭī reports al-Ḍaḥḥāk's Omani gloss."}
{"position":"12:36/q21/p4","rows":["BURHAN:v2p277/r12"],"prefer":[],"against":[],"reasons_add":"Al-Zarkashī reports Ibn ʿAzīz's proposal that the transferred usage lies in the verb aʿṣiru, meaning to extract."}
{"position":"12:36/q20/p1","rows":["BURHAN:v2p277/r12","BINTSHATI-IJAZ:p415/r3","BINTSHATI-IJAZ:p416/r3"],"prefer":[],"against":[],"reasons_add":"Ibn ʿAzīz glosses aʿṣiru as extract. Bint al-Shāṭiʾ traces ʿaṣr forms to pressure and extraction, comparing the vine, harvest year, rain clouds, whirlwind, and al-ʿAṣr."}
{"question":"12:36/q23","position":"The mention of bread anticipates the grain that birds actually eat.","reasons":"Al-Zarkashī says the dreamer names bread although birds eat grain, by naming it for what the grain will become.","rows":["BURHAN:v2p277/r8"],"prefer":[],"against":[]}
{"position":"12:36/q02/p2","rows":["BURHAN:v4p426/r3","ITQAN:v2p516#3/r2"],"prefer":[],"against":[],"reasons_add":"Al-Zarkashī says maʿa marks shared participation in an action or ruling without necessarily requiring simultaneity; al-Suyūṭī cites association apart from shared time or place."}
{"position":"12:36/q02/p1","rows":["ITQAN:v2p516#3/r1"],"prefer":[],"against":[],"reasons_add":"Al-Suyūṭī gives shared time or place as a basic sense of maʿa, while analyzing it as a noun."}
{"position":"12:36/q03/p1","rows":["ITQAN:v2p516#3/r4"],"prefer":[],"against":[],"reasons_add":"Al-Suyūṭī reports al-Rāghib's point that the complement of maʿa receives the intended focus."}
{"position":"12:36/q29/p1","rows":["NASHR:v1p390#4/r2","NASHR:v1p390#4/r3","NASHR:v1p390#4/r4","NASHR:v1p390#4/r5","NASHR:v1p390#4/r6","NASHR:v1p390#4/r7","NASHR:v1p390#4/r10","NASHR:v1p392/r2"],"prefer":["NASHR:v1p390#4/r6"],"against":[],"reasons_add":"Ibn al-Jazarī details Abu Jaʿfar's disputed routes for tahqīq of nabbiʾnā; Abū Ṭāhir, al-Hudhalī, Abū al-ʿIzz, Abū al-ʿAlā, and Ibn Mihrān transmit or discuss retention. Al-Aṣbahānī's Warsh route excepts nabbiʾ forms from substitution."}
{"position":"12:36/q29/p2","rows":["NASHR:v1p390#4/r1","NASHR:v1p390#4/r2","NASHR:v1p390#4/r4","NASHR:v1p390#4/r5","NASHR:v1p390#4/r7"],"prefer":[],"against":[],"reasons_add":"Ibn al-Jazarī explains Abū Jaʿfar's replacement of silent hamza with a preceding-vowel-matched long vowel and records substitution of nabbiʾnā through some routes."}
{"position":"12:36/q04/p1","rows":["NASHR:v2p295/r4"],"prefer":["NASHR:v2p295/r4"],"against":[],"reasons_add":"Ibn al-Jazarī says all readers agree on kasra at 12:36 and related prison mentions; the fatḥa of Yaʿqūb belongs to 12:33 and marks the verbal noun."}
{"position":"12:36/q04/p2","rows":[],"prefer":[],"against":["NASHR:v2p295/r4"],"reasons_add":""}
{"position":"12:36/q18/p2","rows":["NASHR:v2p163#2/r1","NASHR:v2p296/r4","NASHR:v2p296/r5","NASHR:v2p296/r10"],"prefer":[],"against":[],"reasons_add":"Ibn al-Jazarī lists the two dream phrases among Yūsuf's open yāʾs and names the Medinan readers, Ibn Kathīr, and Abū ʿAmr in the relevant lists."}
{"position":"12:36/q19/p2","rows":["NASHR:v2p163#2/r1","NASHR:v2p296/r10"],"prefer":[],"against":[],"reasons_add":"Ibn al-Jazarī counts the two innī arānī expressions among the sūra's yāʾs before open hamza and records their opening among the Yūsuf forms."}
